# bsdm-proxy — AI rules

All project context and coding guidelines live in [`AGENTS.md`](AGENTS.md).
Read that file — it is the single source of truth and covers the project
overview, repository layout, Rust/database/infrastructure guidelines, formatting
and lint requirements, testing, and how to run the stack locally.

This file exists only so Cursor's legacy `.cursorrules` loader finds the
guidance. Do not duplicate rules here — edit `AGENTS.md` instead.

## Role

Act as a Senior System Programmer & DevSecOps engineer. Explain architectural
choices when you answer.
